<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.12.4: Possible Equation for a Function on a Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01468</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.12.4: Possible Equation for a Function on a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6729ab16-b788-4137-ac3b-733b3dabef62</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Examine the three graphs representing three exponential functions: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">
          <media alt="">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_14_09_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00003">The functions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are defined as:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></item>
        <item><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></item>
      </list>

        <exercise id="_8349eeef-9ab1-4105-bcd7-065b0c411f0f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">Which of the following could define function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
            <para id="para-00005">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00006"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00007"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2.5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00008"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3.5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00009"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4.5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            
            <para id="para-00010">Nice try! The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2.5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      
        <exercise id="exer-00001">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00011">Explain your reasoning.</para>
            <para id="para-00012">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00014">The graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> has the same <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept as the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, which is 20. It grows more quickly than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> but more slowly than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>,<emphasis effect="italics"> </emphasis>so the growth factor must be greater than 2 but less than 4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
    </section>
  </content></document>
